  "notes": "Term-by-term sequence transcribed verbatim from the official 2025-2026 Arkansas Tech University Catalog, 'Music, Bachelor of Arts' curriculum (pp. 200-202), a genuine institution-published semester sequence. To meet the requirements for the baccalaureate degree in music, the student must complete 120 semester hours, including: 8 hours of applied music and successful completion of the Applied Competency and Keyboard Proficiency Exams; 4 hours in major ensembles (band or choir); 16 hours in music theory and ear training; and 9 hours of music history. An audition, demonstrating acceptable musical preparation, is required prior to enrollment as a major in music. Catalog footnote 1: see appropriate alternatives or substitutions in General Education Requirements (p. 75). Catalog footnote 2: see course descriptions for the appropriate applied music course number (the 'MUS_1__2' slots below are applied music, 2 hours per catalog). Catalog footnote 3: class piano or applied piano must be taken each semester until successful completion of Piano Proficiency. Catalog footnote 4: Applied Competency is required for enrollment in upper-level applied study for two-hour credit and for completion of all music degrees. Catalog footnote 5: concurrent enrollment in a major ensemble is required to be eligible to enroll in applied study; only one credit per semester may be used to fulfill the major ensemble requirement — the select-one major-ensemble slot per term is seeded as a single choice slot per catalog. Catalog footnote 6: at least 66 hours must be non-music hours (26 hours General Education courses, 6 hours Foreign Language courses, and 34 hours Elective courses). Catalog footnote 7: at least 40 of the 120 hours required for graduation must be earned in 3000-4000 level courses. Catalog footnote 8: all minimum college hours (at least two semesters) should be in one language; students may waive three hours of language requirement for every one year of language study in high school with grades of 'C' or better. Zero-credit items (MUS 1000/MUS 3000 Recital Attendance, MUS 1440 Piano Proficiency, MUS 2000 Applied Competency) are required degree milestones and carry required_zero:true. Machine prereqs omitted (prereq: []) — the curriculum page prints no per-course prerequisites. tccns mirrors the local ATU course code; transfer_confidence core_only. Coordinator note (2026-10-01): allow_repeated_courses=true. The catalog genuinely requires the same courses in multiple semesters: MUS 1000/MUS 3000 Recital Attendance (0-credit, required each semester), a major ensemble each semester (footnote 9: only one ensemble credit per semester may count; select-one slots seeded as single choice slots with the catalog's slash notation, verbatim course codes preserved in options), and applied-music study each semester (MUS 1202 Piano / MUS 1232 Voice / MUS 1501 Band as applicable; instrument-specific numbers per catalog footnote 2). These are true repeats of the same requirement, not transcription errors.",
